# q-at (plan section 6, M6): Q under the pointer at x = −1.5. The plane is (488, 92, 936 x 792) at
# 1440 x 900, its origin at (468, 396) in it at 50 px a unit, so x = −1.5 is the plane's 393, the
# page's 881; the pointer at (881, 376) is on the empty plane (no mark's hit box), so Q follows it
# on P's 0.01 lattice: Q (−1.50, 2.25) with its ring, its label held up-right, its dashed guide
# (1 px, 4 6) full height and its drop lines (1.5 px, 5 4) to both axes; the Points card's Q row
# reads it.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
move 881 376
# Q enters over 160 ms, its drop lines growing (FV 05, M10's motion): the shot waits it out.
wait 500
shot q-at
